## app_crud Tool - App Management

The `app_crud` tool manages Puck visual apps.

### Methods
| Method | Description | Required Params |
|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| list | List all apps | - |
| read | Get app by ID | app_id |
| create | Create new app | data.name |
| update | Update app settings | app_id, data |
| delete | Delete app (cascades) | app_id |

### App Fields
- `id`: Unique app identifier
- `name`: Display name (required for create)
- `slug`: URL-friendly identifier (auto-generated if not provided)
- `description`: What the app does
- `themeConfig`: Theme settings (JSON: primaryColor, secondaryColor, etc.)
- `homePageId`: Default landing page ID

### Example Usage
```python
# List all apps
result = app_crud(method="list")

# Get an app
result = app_crud(method="read", app_id=1)

# Create an app
result = app_crud(method="create", data={"name": "My App", "description": "..."})

# Update an app
result = app_crud(method="update", app_id=1, data={"name": "New Name"})

# Delete an app (WARNING: deletes all pages too)
result = app_crud(method="delete", app_id=1)
```

### Response Format (TOON)
- Success: `app:created,1,My App,my-app` or `apps|5]{id,name,slug}:...`
- Failure: `FAILED: error message`
